JavaScript (JS) is a lightweight, interpreted programming language used primarily
 to create dynamic and interactive content on websites.Alongside HTML (which structures web content) 
 and CSS (which handles the design and layout), JavaScript serves as the third core technology
  of the World Wide Web. It was originally created by Brendan Eich in 1995 for the Netscape browser 
  but has since evolved into a versatile language capable of running on servers, mobile devices, and more.